      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I was saying that think of it like a team of skilled craftsmen, each one working together to build a magnificent structure, in this case, muscle tissue. The leucine is like the master builder, directing the team and ensuring that the materials are used efficiently. The mTOR pathway is like the construction site, where all the necessary components are assembled to create the final product - muscle growth.\n\nAnd, just as a skilled craftsman needs the right tools and materials, the body needs the right balance of nutrients to support muscle growth. A caloric surplus provides the necessary energy, but it's the specific macronutrient balance that determines the outcome. Too much protein can lead to an imbalance, like a builder using too much mortar and not enough sand, resulting in a structure that's unstable and prone to collapse.\n\nIn the context of nitrogen balance, a caloric surplus can lead to an increase in protein synthesis, but if the body is not able to utilize the excess protein efficiently, it can lead to an imbalance, like a team of craftsmen working at cross-purposes, resulting in a structure that's not as strong as it could be.",
